From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joinery <joinery@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:01:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Ask which tools make a project while creating it

Creating a project is the moment the tools that will make it get chosen, so
the dialog has two pages now: Godot's own fields, then Joinery's
questionnaire. Next moves between them and Create finishes, which keeps the
whole decision in the Project Manager rather than deferring it to the editor.

The questionnaire is built from `joinery tools --json`, so the catalog and
its admission rules stay the one source of truth and this code cannot invent
a tool or offer one whose server is not built. Required tools cannot be
unticked, unavailable ones cannot be ticked, and each carries the catalog's
own reason as its tooltip.

Creating then installs the addon and runs `joinery setup` with the chosen
tools, which is the path `joinery new` takes.

All of it degrades: with no Joinery install the page is skipped, the title
and button read as stock Godot, and the user gets a plain valid project.
Only in that case is `joinery/setup_pending` set, so the addon asks in the
editor instead; when the questionnaire has already run, it does not nag.

Joinery-only, not for upstream: it reroutes a stock flow into Joinery's own.
---
